// EXPECT: [E100]
// EXPECT-TEXT: Error Ln 8, Col 1: `c_include` is not supported: an `extern` declaration carries its own C prototype, which the emitted C declares; a header's declarations would contradict it (spec 17). Remove the line.
// `c_include` was parsed and dropped: no header reached the emitted C, and one that does not
// exist was accepted. Emitting it is wrong too, because a header's prototypes contradict the
// ones the emitted C declares for each `extern`. It was the smoke test c_include_smoke_pass.ln,
// which printed through `libc_puts` with or without the line.

c_include "<stdio.h>"

extern func libc_puts(s *u8) i32 effects io

func main() effects io {
    libc_puts("Hello from c_include!")
}
